        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 18:05:08.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 osp: do not wait out a disconnect nobody answers",
        "message": "LU-20076 osp: do not wait out a disconnect nobody answers\n\nWhen an MDT stops, each OSP sends a DISCONNECT to its OST or\nMDT and the shutdown waits for the reply. If that target was\nstopped first and its node has no service left, as when\nconf-sanity stops the OSTs and then the MDTs, the request is\ndropped on arrival and the MDT waits for its timeout: the\nconnect timeout plus the network latency estimate, about 10\nseconds with at_min=5. conf-sanity and other suites pay this on\nmost MDT unmounts.\n\nA peer that is up replies at once, and acts on the request\nwhether or not the reply is awaited. Wait one second for the\nreply, then abort the request and ignore its result. A request\nnot yet sent by then is lost, and the peer keeps the export\nuntil it evicts it, as it does today when the timeout expires.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: testlist=replay-single,recovery-small\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0bedaf7309555d642795ec72e26ef3085a8d3131\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
